WEBVTT

00:02:28.044 --> 00:02:31.435
to find out what moves you most,

00:02:31.435 --> 00:02:34.779
to recall where your truest happiness lies

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:36.549
and to remember that sometimes

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:39.264
making a living and making a life

00:02:39.264 --> 00:02:42.447
point in opposite directions.

00:02:42.457 --> 00:02:45.654
And of course, this is what wise beings
through the centuries

00:02:45.654 --> 00:02:47.897
from every tradition have been telling us.

00:02:47.897 --> 00:02:49.823
It's an old idea.

00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:53.117
More than 2,000 years ago, 
the Stoics were reminding us

00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:56.171
it's not our experience
that makes our lives,

00:02:56.171 --> 00:02:58.379
it's what we do with it.

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:02.231
Imagine a hurricane suddenly 
sweeps through your town